      "body": "## Summary\n\nFix incorrect bus bandwidth calculations for collectives operating on subgroups.\n\n- Propagate the collective process group through `timed_op()` to the communication logger.\n- Calculate bus bandwidth using the participating process group's size.\n- Preserve compatibility for callers that omit the group and keep world-group record names unchanged.\n- Separate summary records for different subgroup sizes.\n- Add regression coverage for subgroup bandwidth calculations, summary separation, and process-group propagation.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Isolated communication-logger tests: 8 passed, 2 warnings.\n- Python syntax validation: passed.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n- Normal pytest collection is blocked by the missing `cpuinfo` dependency.\n- The wrapper-level regression test has not yet been executed successfully through normal pytest collection.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis PR addresses the subgroup bandwidth calculation and summary separation described in #8861. Distinguishing different process groups of the same size and subgroup-aware straggler analysis remain out of scope.\n\nFixes #8861\n",
